From 7292e9bad2edf25d38a0bf4b358ec6857da27bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hang(Harry) Gao <GaohRyan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:14:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] terrain: height scan through the imagination (replay
 origin, compiled step, rollout, critic); root-height feature measured from
 the mean terrain under the body

Every replay row carries the env origin of its episode, so the scan of a stored or imagined state can be looked up
from the global height map. The imagined rollout re-queries the scan at every predicted state; the actor sees a
noisy copy, the world model and the critic the clean one.

Checked locally with the line G session-3 checkpoint (expanded networks): on a flat map the rollout equals the
flat-ground code path under the same seed (max reward difference 1.5e-8, states identical); on the generated
20 cm pyramid the rollout, the lifted rewards and the backward pass run and the gradient reaches the new scan
columns of the decoder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
